# Dual-path architecture: unified pipeline + operations Ask LEO

Post-processing layers (lab-value guard, scope guard, observable normalisation,
entity-type normalisation, value-unit linking, ConText, situation lookup, and
the disorder gate) are shared via `libs/pipeline/post_processing.py`
(`run_post_processing()`).  Both the training and runtime pipelines call this
single function.  Any change to a post-processing layer is automatically
applied to BOTH paths.

Changes to assertions, semantic tags, LLM prompt rules, or the escalation
flow still require updating BOTH the unified pipeline AND the Ask LEO /
escalation path, since escalation runs independently of post-processing.

## Unified post-processing pipeline (shared)

All 9 layers live in `libs/pipeline/post_processing.py`.

| Layer | Module |
|-------|--------|
| 1 -- Post-Processor Rules | `libs/ner/post_processor_rules.py` |
| 2 -- Lab-Value Guard | `libs/ner/lab_value_guard.py` |
| 3 -- Scope Guard | `libs/ner/scope_guard.py` |
| 4 -- Observable Normalisation | `libs/ner/observable_post_processor.py` |
| 5 -- Entity-Type Normalisation | `libs/pipeline/post_processing.py` (`normalise_entity_types`) |
| 6 -- Value-Unit Linking | `libs/pipeline/post_processing.py` (`link_observable_value_units`) |
| 7 -- ConText Assertion Detection | `libs/ner/context_engine.py` |
| 8 -- Situation Lookup Normalisation | `libs/ner/context_detector.py` |
| 9 -- Disorder Gate (optional) | `libs/llm_client/disorder_verifier.py` |

## Consumers of `run_post_processing()`

| Consumer | File |
|----------|------|
| Runtime pipeline | `services/coding_worker/app/pipeline/pipeline_service.py` (`_run_unified_post_processing`) |
| Training / label verifier | `services/api/app/services/label_verifier.py` (`_process_label`) |

## Path 2 -- /operations Ask LEO (review UI)

Processes CodingReview nodes when a reviewer clicks "Ask LEO".

| Layer | File |
|-------|------|
| Escalation prompts | `libs/llm_client/escalation.py` (`_CANDIDATES_SYSTEM`, `escalate_coding`) |
| Ask LEO smart endpoint | `services/api/app/routers/training.py` (`ask_leo_smart`) |
| Ask LEO rank endpoint | `services/api/app/routers/training.py` (`ask_leo_rank_candidates`, inline prompt) |
| Disorder verifier | `libs/llm_client/disorder_verifier.py` (`_SYSTEM_PROMPT`) |
| Assertion notes | `services/api/app/routers/training.py` (`_ASSERTION_NOTES`) |
| Assertion validation | `services/api/app/routers/training.py` (`_VALID_ASSERTIONS`) |
| Label verifier | `services/api/app/services/label_verifier.py` (`_AUTO_CODE_BLOCKED`, `_ASSERTION_QUEUE_SET`) |

## Shared graph + UI

| Layer | File |
|-------|------|
| Document writes | `libs/cypher/documents_queries.py` (`_NON_PRESENT`, `_assertion_context`) |
| Coding review queries | `libs/cypher/coding_review_queries.py` (assertion filters) |
| UI assertion options | `services/ui/src/components/operations/CodingReviewCasesModal.tsx` (`ASSERTION_OPTIONS`) |
| UI assertion chips | `services/ui/src/lib/types.ts` (`ASSERTION_CHIP`), `services/ui/src/components/AssertionChip.tsx` |
| Training adapter | `libs/model_registry/training_adapter.py` (`_VALID_ASSERTIONS`) |

## Checklist for ANY assertion / safety-guard / prompt change

1. If it is a post-processing layer change, update the shared module in `libs/pipeline/post_processing.py` (both paths inherit automatically)
2. Update the runtime extraction prompt (`libs/prompts/extraction_v1.py`)
3. Update the escalation prompts (`libs/llm_client/escalation.py`)
4. Update the ask-leo-rank inline prompt (`training.py`)
5. Update ALL `_VALID_ASSERTIONS` sets (at least 3 locations)
6. Update `_AUTO_CODE_BLOCKED` sets (at least 2 locations)
7. Update `_ASSERTION_QUEUE_SET` if the assertion needs human review
8. Update `_assertion_context()` in `documents_queries.py`
9. Update `_NON_PRESENT` if the assertion should block patient-level shortcuts
10. Update assertion review queue Cypher filters if needed
11. Update UI: `ASSERTION_OPTIONS`, `ASSERTION_CHIP`, `AssertionChip.tsx`
12. Update ConText engine if the assertion can be detected from text patterns
13. Add tests covering both paths (parity tests in `tests/test_pipeline_parity.py`)
